  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Over an array, TEXTSPLIT and REGEXEXTRACT keep only the first piece of each element",
  "statement": "When TEXTSPLIT's text is an array, even a 1 by 1 array, the call lifts over the elements and each returns only its first piece. MAP over the same lambda gives #CALC!, while BYROW gives the first pieces. REGEXEXTRACT lifted over return_mode does the same, and mode 2 on a pattern with no capture group gives #VALUE!.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "22 recorded TEXTSPLIT and REGEXEXTRACT readings, questions 049 to 093.",
